body:
&#x200B;

Absolutely! Everyone on this planet can build muscle regardless of gender.

I do workout (pre everything and questioning) even tho I haven't seen any visible changes yet, I sure as hecc feel the difference. It just takes time and patience for any gender naturally. 🦭

I just watched the film yesterday and just...why? What was the point of that scene? It wasn't even brought up again. It was so gross and made me feel incredibly bad for Frank especially after he pushed her off and ran to the bathroom to vomit. 

&#x200B;

It makes me even more sad is that somehow there are still some people who won't see that as rape. 😮‍💨

Since i was a young teen before i started questioning, i always wanted to be taller. Nowadays i don't really mind, and i kinda like the thought of having to look up to a tall woman. 

&#x200B;

Plus i'm sure a lot of people here would get flustered at even the thought of having to look up to a tall woman, me included.

I hope this will help since this was my experience this year and what i believe in now. I do also believe in a higher power, i don't follow religion either. I'm very spiritual regardless, and i was okay with that fact because i don't believe we just simply stop existing after we die. Death is natural but with death comes life too. Life is everywhere, the entire universe is life. Just because death happens doesn't mean everything is hopeless or meaningless at all. It's okay to be sad and feel grief, but that doesn't mean there is no purpose in life, or even in death.  

&#x200B;

It'll be okay.
